faces","text":"an earlier draft treated the spine width as complete; later turns supersede that, and the current state is a tested candidate awaiting the owner's go-ahead.","section":"How it works","links":[],"cites":["pplx://sessions/cd8ff1ae-b085-bc48-86df-3f5d014fec2f","pplx://sessions/75c42589-77b7-6b68-dc1b-0cf76c6a7b80"]},{"id":"projects/paper-moons-publishing#4","page":"projects/paper-moons-publishing","lead":"One continuity note, two surfaces","text":"the continuity note credits per spread and surfaces a plain warning when the review page is missing. Manual confirmation is still required.","section":"How it works","links":[],"cites":[]},{"id":"projects/paper-moons-publishing#5","page":"projects/paper-moons-publishing","lead":"One character sheet, two surfaces","text":"Sam chose to keep the character sheet and the night cover distinct so neither substitutes for the other. The decision was recorded with the session that produced it.","section":"How it works","links":[],"cites":["pplx://sessions/2b164095-6f02-824f-df4e-2166ede18709","pplx://sessions/75c42589-77b7-6b68-dc1b-0cf76c6a7b80"]},{"id":"projects/paper-moons-publishing#6","page":"projects/paper-moons-publishing","lead":"Spine width survives rollback","text":"an earlier draft treated the spine width as complete; later turns supersede that, and the current state is a tested candidate awaiting the owner's go-ahead.","section":"How it works","links":[],"cites":["https://git.example.test/sam-vale/paper-moons-site/pull/29"]},{"id":"projects/paper-moons-publishing#7","page":"projects/paper-moons-publishing","lead":"Separate character sheet ownership","text":"character sheet changes are reviewed before merge; a passing check across four books is bounded evidence, not proof that the proof copy works for every user.","section":"How it works","links":[],"cites":["https://git.example.test/sam-vale/paper-moons-site/pull/29","pplx://sessions/75c42589-77b7-6b68-dc1b-0cf76c6a7b80"]},{"id":"projects/paper-moons-publishi